# TUXEDO InfinityBook Pro 14 Gen10 AMD (Ryzen AI 9 HX 370)
# Workaround: the AMD USB4 complex at PCI slot 0000:67:00.* exposes FOUR
# functions (one physical chip, one per xHCI/router role):
#   .0  1022:151f  xHCI - internal-only devices (Genesys hub, Bluetooth)
#   .3  1022:151a  xHCI - external USB-C port 1
#   .4  1022:151b  xHCI - external USB-C port 2
#   .6  1022:151d  USB4/Thunderbolt router
# Originally only .0 was pinned (2026-08-25) after it spammed:
#   xhci_hcd 0000:67:00.0: Refused to change power state from D0 to D3hot
# every ~1.2s post-resume. .3/.4 stayed on runtime PM ("auto") and were
# never protected -- turned out to be the ones actually driving the two
# USB-C ports, and they're the ones behind the external-monitor/dock USB
# devices dropping and re-enumerating (whole hub tree disconnects, new
# device numbers) independent of which port or cable is used. Widened to
# the whole 67:00.* function group 2026-09-16 since both external-port
# functions share the same silicon and firmware as the already-confirmed-
# bad .0 function.
# No functional downside: all USB ports keep working; USB devices still
# autosuspend individually. See linux_root/README.md for the "is it fixed
# yet?" test and removal instructions.
#
# Install: sudo cp <this file> /etc/udev/rules.d/ && sudo udevadm control --reload
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x1022", ATTR{device}=="0x151f", ATTR{power/control}="on"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x1022", ATTR{device}=="0x151a", ATTR{power/control}="on"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x1022", ATTR{device}=="0x151b", ATTR{power/control}="on"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x1022", ATTR{device}=="0x151d", ATTR{power/control}="on"
